WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:08.016
This is the other way to connect Discord. You create one bot, then pick each channel from a list instead of pasting an address for every one.

00:00:08.216 --> 00:00:15.286
Open the Discord Developer Portal from the link in the guide. Press New Application, give it a name, and create it.

00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:22.300
In the left menu open Bot. Press Reset Token, then copy the token. Discord only shows it once.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:32.685
Open OAuth2, then the URL Generator. Tick bot. Then tick View Channels, Send Messages, and Embed Links. Open the link it generates, and add the bot to your server.

00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:42.664
On the settings page, open Prefer a bot, paste the token, and press Save Discord. Press Connect and load channels, pick a channel for each report, and save again.

00:00:42.864 --> 00:00:48.931
That is your Discord bot connected. You can change which channel each report goes to at any time.
